---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Net Cloud Edge — Recruiting & Staffing
description: Recruiting and staffing for students starting out and professionals moving on — plus the employers who hire both.
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/logo-fallback.js
  - /assets/js/tabs.js
  - /assets/js/text-rotator.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   HOME

   Order is a funnel, not a feature list. It answers, in sequence, the
   four questions a first-time visitor actually asks:

     1. Who is this for?      hero → dual-path split
     2. What do they do?      services grid → value proposition
     3. Does it work?         growth table → case study → statements → feed
     4. What happens next?    process tabs → CTA

   Proof is deliberately held back until after the offer is understood —
   numbers shown to someone who doesn't yet know what we sell are just
   decoration. Structure per PRD.md; every claim tier per the same file.
   ================================================================ #}

{# ---------- 1. Hero — centred, full measure, image below.

     No ticker strip above it: the hero opens the page directly. The live-activity
     signal it used to carry now sits in the placement feed further down, where a
     reader who has been given a reason to care about it can actually read it
     standing still. ---------- #}
{% include "partials/home-hero.njk" %}

{# ---------- 2. Employer wall — immediately under the hero, where it does
     the most work: recognisable names are the fastest credibility signal
     on the page, and they cost the reader nothing to parse. ---------- #}
{% set placedAtTitle = "Referenced employers" %}
{% set placedAtLead = "Placements closed with these companies." %}
{% include "partials/placed-at.njk" %}

{# ---------- 3. The dual-path split — the page's thesis.

     Two full panels rather than two small cards: this is the single most
     important choice the visitor makes, so it gets a photograph, five
     concrete benefits, and its own CTA on each side. The two sides are
     structurally identical — same shape, same count, same weight — because
     the whole positioning is that we serve both properly, and any asymmetry
     here would quietly contradict that. ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-head is-centered">
    <p class="eyebrow">Two doors</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Which side of the table are you on?</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy">
      Both doors lead to the same team. What changes is who does the work for whom.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-8">
    {% for path in paths.list %}
    <div class="glass-panel flex flex-col overflow-hidden">
      <img src="{{ path.image.src | url }}" alt="{{ path.image.alt }}"
           width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy"
           class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover">

      <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-6 sm:p-8">
        <span class="file-tag w-fit">{{ path.label }}</span>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink">
          {{ path.headline }}
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 body-copy">{{ path.lead }}</p>

        {# Not numbered: these are five parallel benefits, not a sequence. #}
        <ul class="mt-6 flex-1 space-y-4 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
          {% for benefit in path.benefits %}
          <li class="flex gap-3.5">
            <span class="icon-chip-accent mt-0.5 flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg">
              {{ icon(benefit.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}
            </span>
            <span>
              <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ benefit.title }}</span>
              <span class="mt-1 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/60">{{ benefit.text }}</span>
            </span>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        <a href="{{ path.cta.href | url }}" class="btn-primary mt-8 w-full sm:w-fit">
          {{ path.cta.label }} {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 4. Services grid — six tiles on a paper band.

     The tone shift to `paper` separates the catalogue from the argument
     either side of it without introducing a new colour. Five services plus
     a router tile, so the third row never ends on an orphan. ---------- #}
<section class="border-y border-border bg-paper py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we do</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Five services, one pipeline.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="meta max-w-xs leading-relaxed">Source → vet → place → verify → upskill</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {% for service in services.list %}
      <a href="{{ service.url | url }}" class="glass-panel card-lift group flex flex-col p-6 sm:p-7">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="icon-chip">{{ icon(service.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          {# ink/65, matching .meta — the ref reads as quiet detailing but is still real
             text a screen reader will announce, so it holds the 4.5:1 body threshold
             rather than the 3:1 decorative one. #}
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink/65">{{ service.ref }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card-title mt-5">{{ service.title }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 flex-1 body-copy">{{ service.shortDescription }}</p>
        <span class="file-tag mt-5 w-fit">
          {%- if service.audience.students %}Students{% endif -%}
          {%- if service.audience.professionals %}{% if service.audience.students %} · {% endif %}Professionals{% endif -%}
          {%- if service.audience.employers %}{% if service.audience.students or service.audience.professionals %} · {% endif %}Employers{% endif -%}
        </span>
        <span class="mt-5 link-arrow">
          Learn more {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
        </span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}

      {# Router tile — fills the sixth slot and catches anyone still comparing,
         pointing at the one thing no competitor builds cleanly: the matrix. #}
      <a href="{{ '/services/' | url }}"
         class="card-lift group flex flex-col justify-between rounded-2xl border border-brand/20 bg-brand/5 p-6 sm:p-7">
        <div>
          <span class="icon-chip">{{ icon("target", "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          <h3 class="card-title mt-5">Not sure which one?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 body-copy">
            One table, all five services, mapped against who each is actually built for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="mt-5 link-arrow">
          Compare all five {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 5. Value proposition — the standing policy.

     Centred statement, then four mechanisms. Each tile names something we
     actually do, not an adjective: "a recruiter who's read your resume"
     rather than "personalised". Adjectives are what every competitor in this
     market writes, which is exactly why they no longer signal anything. #}
<section class="section-container py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-head is-centered">
    <p class="eyebrow">Standing policy</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Four things every placement follows.</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy">
      Not values on a wall. Four commitments that hold on every file we open, and that
      you can hold us to.
    </p>
  </div>

  {% set policies = [
    { icon: "users", t: "Personalised matching", d: "A recruiter who has actually read your resume, not a keyword filter with a friendly name." },
    { icon: "shield", t: "Verified employers", d: "Every partner company is vetted before you are ever introduced to it." },
    { icon: "support", t: "One thread, one recruiter", d: "No chasing status across four job boards and three inboxes. One person owns your file." },
    { icon: "heart", t: "End to end, past the offer", d: "We stay involved through negotiation and check in ninety days after you start." }
  ] %}
  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {% for policy in policies %}
    <div class="glass-panel card-lift flex flex-col p-6">
      <span class="icon-chip">{{ icon(policy.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
      <h3 class="card-title mt-5">{{ policy.t }}</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 body-copy">{{ policy.d }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 6. Proof, in descending order of how checkable it is:
     a dated series, then one traced placement, then signed statements. ---------- #}
<section class="border-y border-border bg-paper py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    {% include "partials/growth-table.njk" %}

    {# 6b — One file traced end to end. The same person as the pull-quote, which is
       why Priya is excluded from the statements row further down. #}
    <div id="case-study" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 sm:mt-16">
      <div class="glass-panel overflow-hidden">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-5">
          <figure class="lg:col-span-2">
            <img src="{{ '/assets/images/home/interview-conversation.jpg' | url }}"
                 alt="A candidate meeting a hiring manager"
                 width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy"
                 class="h-full min-h-[16rem] w-full object-cover">
          </figure>

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 lg:col-span-3 lg:p-10">
            <span class="status-chip"><span class="status-dot"></span>Placement closed</span>
            <h2 class="mt-5 font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">
              Forty applications, no replies. Sixteen days after her first call, an offer.
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-4 body-copy">
              Priya's résumé buried a strong analytics background on page two. We rebuilt the
              profile, matched her to three employers who needed exactly that, and prepped her
              for every interview.
            </p>
            <p class="highlight mt-6">The role fit better than anything I'd found on my own.</p>

            <dl class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-4 gap-4 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
              {% for fact in [
                { k: "Day 0", v: "Applied" },
                { k: "Day 4", v: "Matched" },
                { k: "Day 11", v: "Interview" },
                { k: "Day 16", v: "Offer" }
              ] %}
              <div>
                <dt class="meta">{{ fact.k }}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-1 font-grotesk text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-base">{{ fact.v }}</dd>
              </div>
              {% endfor %}
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# 6c — Signed statements. Horizontal swipe on mobile, four across on desktop.
       Initials avatars, not stock headshots: a stranger's face beside a real quote
       is the exact move that costs a trust page its trust. #}
    <div id="statements" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-28 sm:mt-16">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Signed statements</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">On record, from both sides.</h2>
      </div>

      {% set featured = [] %}
      {% for t in testimonials.list %}
        {% if t.slug != "priya" and featured.length < 4 %}{% set _ = featured.push(t) %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      <div class="mt-8 -mx-4 flex snap-x snap-mandatory gap-5 overflow-x-auto px-4 pb-2 sm:mx-0 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-2 sm:overflow-visible sm:px-0 sm:pb-0 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {% for testimonial in featured %}
        <div class="w-[82%] shrink-0 snap-start sm:w-auto">
          {% include "partials/testimonial-card.njk" %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 7. What happens next — the two processes, tabbed ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% include "partials/path-tabs.njk" %}
</section>

{# ---------- 8. The live feed — last piece of proof before the ask ---------- #}
{% include "partials/placement-feed.njk" %}

{# ---------- 9. Close the loop ---------- #}
{% set ctaHeadline = "Ready to find your footing?" %}
{% set ctaSubtext = "Whether you're job hunting or hiring, the first conversation is free — and it starts the system tracking your file." %}
{% set ctaLabel = "Get Started" %}
{% set ctaHref = "/contact/" %}
{% include "partials/cta-section.njk" %}
